  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 220 PM CDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nUpper level ridging will amplify by early weekend with the ridge \naxis approaching from the west. Broad upper troughing will remain \nstalled out across the Hudson Bay with a second disturbance lifting \ninto the Pacific Northwest. This should result in ridge breakdown as \na lead shortwave ejects out of Wyoming. The result of this will be \nincreased rain and thunderstorms again, favoring late Saturday into \nSunday. Flow will generally flatten out as this Pacific Northwest \ndisturbance begins to translate across southern Canada by early \nnext week. A trailing frontal boundary with reinforcing high \npressure should traverse the area towards the middle of the week. \nThis will sustain daily rain and thunderstorm chances while keeping \ntemperatures more on the seasonable side (average highs for late \nAugust are low to middle 80s). Should this pattern hold, recurring \nrain chances will bring about potential for at least locally \nbeneficial rainfall to some drought stricken areas. Details remain \nfar from certain so continue to check back with later forecasts.",
